    {
      \"path\": \"src/cli/commands/item.ts\",
      \"line\": 787,
      \"body\": \"[MUST-FIX] These relationship flags only validate that the ref resolves, but not that the target is a spec item. That means task refs can be linked into "'`relates_to`/`implements`/`depends_on`, which conflicts with existing `link create` behavior (it rejects non-spec targets). Please add a non-task check for each target ref before updating relationships."
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/item-set-relationships.test.ts",
      "line": 75,
      "body": "[MUST-FIX] The linked spec `@item-set` has ACs 1-7, but this PR adds annotations only for ac-5/6/7. I could not find any `// AC: @item-set ac-4` annotation in the suite. Please add an explicit annotated test for ac-4 (`item set --status` updates implementation status), even if the behavior is covered indirectly elsewhere."
    },
    {
      "path": "src/cli/commands/item.ts",
      "line": 813,
      "body": "[SHOULD-FIX] Mutual exclusivity checks run after ref resolution. With conflicting flags plus an invalid ref (e.g. `--relates-to @missing --clear-relates-to`), the command returns NOT_FOUND instead of a usage error for invalid flag combinations. Consider checking exclusivity first for cleaner error semantics."
    }
  ]
}
JSON

cat > /tmp/codex-pr-335-review.md <<'"'MD'
# PR #335 Review

## Verdict
REQUEST_CHANGES

## Findings

### MUST-FIX
1. "'`src/cli/commands/item.ts:787`
Relationship target refs are only checked for existence, not type. `item set --relates-to/--implements/--depends-on` can accept task refs, while `link create` explicitly rejects non-spec targets. This creates inconsistent behavior and can pollute spec-item relationship fields with task references.

2. `tests/item-set-relationships.test.ts:75`
Linked spec `@item-set` has acceptance criteria `ac-1` through `ac-7`, but annotated coverage is missing for `ac-4`. I could not find `// AC: @item-set ac-4` in the test suite. Please add an explicitly annotated test for status updates (`item set --status ...`).

### SHOULD-FIX
1. `src/cli/commands/item.ts:813`
Mutual exclusivity checks happen after reference resolution. For conflicting combinations with invalid refs, users get NOT_FOUND instead of a usage error. Validate mutually exclusive flags before reference lookup to keep error semantics consistent.

## AC Coverage Snapshot (`@item-set`)
- `ac-1`: annotated (`tests/integration.test.ts`)
- `ac-2`: annotated (`tests/integration.test.ts`)
- `ac-3`: annotated (`tests/integration.test.ts`)
- `ac-4`: **missing annotation**
- `ac-5`: annotated (`tests/item-set-relationships.test.ts`)
- `ac-6`: annotated (`tests/item-set-relationships.test.ts`)
- `ac-7`: annotated (`tests/item-set-relationships.test.ts`)

## Test Quality Notes
- New tests are behavior-focused and not fluff.
- Coverage is primarily CLI integration style (appropriate for command semantics).
MD

